<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17299" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exsŭpĕrābĭlis</span></b> 
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exup-</span></b> ),
		e, adj.
		exsupero. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Pass.</i>, <i>that may be
			overcome</i>, <i>surmountable</i>, <i>superable</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non exsuperabile saxum (Sisyphi),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 3, 39</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ingenium mortale,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 1, 214</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>that overcomes</i>, <i>overpowering</i>, <i>irresistible</i>: opera, Quadrig. ap. <i><span class="en">Gell. 17,
				2, 14</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
